---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Advisory · Noah Barlow"
  description="Fractional brand and growth leadership for founder-led challenger companies — embedded strategic partnership rather than outsourced production."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Advisory</p>
      <h1 style="margin-top:1.5rem; max-width: 13ch;">
        Fractional brand &amp; growth leadership.
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        An embedded strategic partner for founder-led companies — senior
        involvement, limited engagements, and a working style that stays close
        enough to the P&amp;L to be useful to it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="s-head">
        <div class="left">
          <span class="eyebrow">Engagement model</span>
          <h2>Built for founders, not for agency rosters.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="right">
          <p>
            I take a small number of engagements per year. Each is sized for
            real strategic involvement: working sessions in the room, brand
            and packaging decisions made with you rather than presented at
            you, and an operating cadence designed to compound over months.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="framework">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">01</div>
          <h3>Diagnostic</h3>
          <p>
            A two-to-four-week strategic audit. Brand, package, retail, and
            demand looked at as a single system — including the things your
            team is too close to see.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">02</div>
          <h3>Engagement</h3>
          <p>
            A six-to-twelve-month embedded retainer. Brand strategy,
            packaging system development, creative direction, and the
            operating cadence to make the change land in market.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">03</div>
          <h3>Board</h3>
          <p>
            For founders who don't need a full retainer: a board-style
            advisory role — monthly strategic counsel, decision support, and
            access between sessions when the stakes call for it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="s-head">
        <div class="left">
          <span class="eyebrow">What I do</span>
          <h2>The work I'm hired to lead.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="right">
          <p>
            Strategic leadership where brand, packaging, and demand have to
            work as one system.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top: 1.2em;">
            Need full agency execution too? I work closely with
            <a href="https://smalleragency.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Smaller Agency</a>
            &mdash; efficient, founder-friendly, built for this kind of work.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="advisory">
        <div>
          <p class="pull">
            Strategy and packaging are the same job. Hiring two firms for
            it is why most launches drift.
          </p>
          <div style="margin-top: 1.5em; color: var(--mute); font-size: var(--t-md); max-width: 36ch;">
            <p>
              I work directly with founders, CEOs, and senior marketing
              leads — not through account layers. The fewer hands, the
              sharper the brand.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li><span class="k">01</span><span class="v">Brand strategy and positioning architecture</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">02</span><span class="v">Packaging systems and shelf psychology</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">03</span><span class="v">Creative direction and category point of view</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">04</span><span class="v">Go-to-market sequencing and launch leadership</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">05</span><span class="v">Retail readiness, trade, and on-premise programs</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">06</span><span class="v">Demand generation strategy and growth systems</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">07</span><span class="v">Founder support and board-level brand counsel</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="s-head">
        <div class="left">
          <span class="eyebrow">Who I work with</span>
          <h2>Founder-led challenger companies.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="right">
          <p>
            Mostly private, mostly founder-led. What they have in common is
            readiness — founders who already know what they don't want to do
            next, and need a senior partner who'll help them commit to what
            they do.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="framework">
        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">CPG</div>
          <h3>Beverage, food, RTD</h3>
          <p>Mass-premium, premium-import, alcohol and non-alc, functional drinks, snacks, frozen.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">WELL</div>
          <h3>Wellness &amp; lifestyle</h3>
          <p>Cannabis, functional wellness, beauty-adjacent, personal care, and emerging consumer.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <div class="num">HOSP</div>
          <h3>Hospitality &amp; retail</h3>
          <p>Founder-led hospitality, concept retail, and DTC brands building a physical presence.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="contact-card">
        <div class="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">Selectively available · 2026</p>
          <h2 style="margin-top:0.85rem;">Two to three engagements per quarter.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="right">
          <p>
            If you're a founder considering a fractional brand or growth
            leader, the next move is a thirty-minute call. Bring the
            problem; I'll bring the framing.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn hot">Book a strategy call</a>
            <a href="/work" class="btn ghost">See case studies</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
